                        "entry_id": "2de7a980-cb1d-3a76-b47c-69dfd8a953d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The young of the Manx shearwater (Puffinus puffinus), especially eaten as food."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fa6fdde-0db6-32f8-8554-f3e98750462d",
                        "entry_id": "2de7a980-cb1d-3a76-b47c-69dfd8a953d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The Atlantic puffin (Fratercula arctica) or (by extension) any of the other various small seabirds of the genera Fratercula and Lunda that are black and white with a brightly-coloured beak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d9c7bf1-8345-48cd-9f0e-98714d18cbc2",
                                "sense_id": "7fa6fdde-0db6-32f8-8554-f3e98750462d",
                                "text": "Naturally the Chickies and the Gooverooskies and the Epatkas—the Burgomaster Gulls and the Kittiwakes and the Puffins, who are always looking for a chance to be rude—took up the cry, and—so Limmershin told me—for nearly five minutes you could not have heard a gun fired on Walrus Islet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "16c6e504-2232-37a1-be1c-41be65446c81",
                        "entry_id": "2de7a980-cb1d-3a76-b47c-69dfd8a953d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various African and Asian pierid butterflies of the genus Appias. Some species of this genus are also known as albatrosses."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
